# BLO-34872. The vendored adapter's per-patch log used to be one append-only
# table, so every PR touching that tree conflicted with every other one on it.
# The fix that works is one file per change in
# `vendor/paperclip-adapter-claude-k8s/PROVENANCE-CHANGES.d/` — two distinct new
# files never conflict under any merge implementation, no driver required.
#
# ⚠ The `merge=union` line below was the FIRST attempt and it does not fix the
# real failure. GitHub's server-side merge ignores .gitattributes merge drivers,
# and that is what computes a PR's `mergeable` state and the merge-queue rebase.
# Measured 2026-09-30 against master `0bb33a1a7`: #2070 and #1459 were ejected
# with `merge_conflict` minutes after #1898 landed a row, while `git merge-tree`
# with these attributes resolved both cleanly. #1699 was ejected three times on
# it after its author had moved its row here *because* of this attribute.
#
# It is kept, not removed: PROVENANCE-CHANGES.md is frozen but still carries
# rows from in-flight PRs, and union still makes a *local* `git rebase` of those
# resolve cleanly. Do not read it as protection. Do not move anything else here:
# a union keeps both sides' added lines, so it cannot reconcile an interior edit
# and cannot choose between two values of a single-valued field — which is why
# BLO-35109 deleted the 64-hex integrity hash rather than relocating it.
# `provenance-union-merge.test.mjs` pins all of this, including a
# driver-disabled merge that reproduces GitHub's behaviour.
#
# BLO-41101 AC5 — DECISION: KEEP, and the guard is what makes that safe.
# This attribute is the mechanism that HID the bug it was meant to fix: because
# a local rebase resolves, #1797's author reproduced "clean" locally while the
# queue ejected the PR six times in 24 days. Removing it was considered and
# rejected. `check-vendored-provenance-log.mjs` now rejects ANY commit in
# base..head that touches this file, so the hiding mechanism has nothing left
# to hide — CI, not the merge driver, is the authority. Removing it would only
# add a second, harder-to-read failure (a local conflict) to branches the guard
# already rejects with a message and a one-command repair, and it would change
# nothing for any branch that does not touch this file. Net zero safety gain,
# non-zero churn. Revisit only when no open PR carries a row here.
# Known-stale by design: the frozen file's own header still says every PR
# "appends a row here". It cannot be corrected, since an edit to it is itself
# a rejected modification. PROVENANCE-CHANGES.d/README.md carries the
# superseding statement.
vendor/paperclip-adapter-claude-k8s/PROVENANCE-CHANGES.md merge=union
